  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A mass oscillating in simple harmonic motion on the end of a spring has an amplitude <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"x\"></span><sub>0</sub> and a total energy E<sub>T</sub>. The mass on the spring is doubled and made to oscillate with the same amplitude <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"x\"></span><sub>0</sub>.</p>\n<p>What is the total energy of the oscillating system after the change?</p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\">E<sub>T</sub></li><li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\sqrt{2}\"></span>E<sub>T</sub></li><li data-label=\"C\">2E<sub>T</sub></li><li data-label=\"D\">4E<sub>T</sub></li></ol>"
  },
